# CI lint before commit

Remote CI runs `pnpm run lint` (`eslint .`) then `pnpm run typecheck` on every push. Do not commit or push until both pass locally. `eslint .` includes `scripts/*.mjs` and `nuxt.config.ts`, not only Vue files.

## Before commit or push

1. Run `pnpm run lint`.
2. Auto-fix if needed: `pnpm exec eslint . --fix`.
3. Re-run `pnpm run lint`. If anything is still red, fix it by hand and do not commit.
4. Run `pnpm run typecheck` as well — CI fails on that next.

## Recurring failures

`@stylistic/arrow-parens`: no parens on a single argument when the body has no braces.

```js
// ❌ BAD
steps.map((step) => step.id)

// ✅ GOOD
steps.map(step => step.id)
steps.map((step) => { return step.id })
```

`nuxt/nuxt-config-keys-order`: keep `nuxt.config.ts` keys in plugin order. `routeRules` must come before `compatibilityDate`. Prefer `pnpm exec eslint nuxt.config.ts --fix` over guessing.

Stylistic config lives in `nuxt.config.ts` (`commaDangle: 'never'`, `braceStyle: '1tbs'`). Match existing files; do not add extra parens, dangling commas, or Allman braces.
